  "notes": "すぐ has three main meanings: immediately (time), easily (manner), and right nearby (distance).\n\nMEANINGS:\n1. Immediately: すぐ{行|い}きます (I'll go right away)\n2. Easily: すぐ{怒|おこ}る (gets angry easily)\n3. Nearby: すぐそこ (right there)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- すぐに: more emphatic form of \"immediately\"\n- すぐ{近|ちか}く: very nearby\n- すぐ{後|あと}で: right after\n- すぐ{前|まえ}に: right in front of\n- すぐそこ: right there (very close)\n\nUSAGE NOTES:\nWhen meaning \"easily,\" すぐ often appears with verbs describing tendencies or habits: すぐ{泣|な}く (cries easily), すぐ{忘|わす}れる (forgets easily).",
